    <p class="intro-lede">
      This policy explains what personal information BatteryCare collects, why we collect it,
      and how it is handled — including data processed through the WhatsApp Business Platform,
      operated by Meta Platforms, Inc. ("Meta"). It applies to our website, our WhatsApp service
      channel, and our engineer and customer onboarding processes.
    </p>

    <section id="introduction">
      <h2><span class="num">1</span>Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        BatteryCare ("we", "us", "our") provides on-demand battery repair and replacement
        services, connecting customers with independent field engineers via WhatsApp and our
        website. Protecting the privacy of everyone who uses our service — customers and
        engineers alike — is a core part of how we operate.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using our WhatsApp service channel, our website, or registering as a BatteryCare
        engineer, you agree to the collection and use of information as described in this
        policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="information-we-collect">
      <h2><span class="num">2</span>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect the following categories of information:</p>
      <h3>From customers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Name and phone number (via WhatsApp)</li>
        <li>Service location or address you share with us</li>
        <li>Details of the service you request (battery type, issue description)</li>
        <li>Payment confirmation details relevant to completing an order</li>
        <li>Messages you send us through WhatsApp, including message content and timestamps</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>From engineers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, phone number, and UPI ID for payouts</li>
        <li>Skills, service area, and experience details provided at registration</li>
        <li>Job acceptance, rejection, and completion activity</li>
        <li>Earnings and payment history</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Automatically collected</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Basic technical metadata associated with WhatsApp message delivery (delivery and read receipts)</li>
        <li>Standard web server logs if you visit our website (IP address, browser type, pages visited)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="whatsapp-platform">
      <h2><span class="num">3</span>WhatsApp &amp; Meta Platform data</h2>
      <p>
        Our service channel runs on the <strong>WhatsApp Business Platform</strong>, a product
        operated by Meta Platforms, Inc. When you message BatteryCare on WhatsApp:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Your messages are transmitted and processed through Meta's infrastructure in order to
          be delivered to us, in accordance with
          <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/business-data-processing-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Meta's Business Data Processing Terms</a> and the
          <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/business-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Meta may process metadata (such as phone number, delivery status, and timestamps) to
          operate the messaging service, secure the platform, and prevent abuse, as described in
          the <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            WhatsApp Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not control, and are not responsible for, Meta's own handling of your data as the
          underlying platform provider. We encourage you to review Meta's policies linked above.
        </li>
        <li>
          We only use WhatsApp message content to operate the BatteryCare service — job requests,
          status updates, and support — and never to sell your data to third parties.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="how-we-use">
      <h2><span class="num">4</span>How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Match customers with available, appropriately skilled engineers</li>
        <li>Send job alerts, status updates, invoices, and payment confirmations via WhatsApp</li>
        <li>Process engineer payouts to the UPI ID provided</li>
        <li>Respond to support requests and resolve disputes</li>
        <li>Maintain the security and reliability of our service</li>
        <li>Comply with applicable legal and regulatory obligations</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="sharing">
      <h2><span class="num">5</span>Sharing your information</h2>
      <p>We share information only in the following limited circumstances:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Between customers and engineers</strong> — so a job can actually be completed (e.g., your location shared with the assigned engineer, and the engineer's name and rating shared with you)</li>
        <li><strong>With Meta</strong> — as a necessary part of operating our WhatsApp service channel, as described in Section 3</li>
        <li><strong>With payment processors</strong> — to complete UPI transactions</li>
        <li><strong>With authorities</strong> — only where required by applicable law, regulation, or valid legal process</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information to advertisers or data brokers.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="retention">
      <h2><span class="num">6</span>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain job, customer, and engineer records for as long as needed to provide the
        service, resolve disputes, and meet our legal and accounting obligations, after which the
        data is deleted or anonymized. WhatsApp message content is retained by us only for as
        long as operationally necessary to support your request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="security">
      <h2><span class="num">7</span>Data security</h2>
      <p>
        We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures — including access controls and
        API key authentication on our systems — to protect the information we hold against
        unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure. No method of transmission or storage,
        however, can be guaranteed to be 100% secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-rights">
      <h2><span class="num">8</span>Your rights &amp; choices</h2>
      <p>Depending on your location, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to the personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your data, subject to legal or operational retention needs</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent to future WhatsApp communications at any time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details in Section 12.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="opt-out">
      <h2><span class="num">9</span>Opting out of WhatsApp messages</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop receiving WhatsApp messages from BatteryCare at any time by replying
        <strong>STOP</strong> to any message, or by blocking our business number directly within
        WhatsApp. Engineers can go offline from job alerts at any time by replying
        <strong>OFFLINE</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="children">
      <h2><span class="num">10</span>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our service is intended for use by individuals aged 18 and above. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children. If you believe a minor has provided us with
        personal data, please contact us so we can remove it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2><span class="num">11</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for
        legal, operational, or regulatory reasons. The "Effective" date at the top of this page
        indicates when the current version took effect. Material changes will be communicated
        through our website or WhatsApp channel where appropriate.
      </p>
    </section>

